title ALES193 — Lotus's stereo_reverb_mix: the wet/dry balance carried across a stereo master — snapshot both dry channels, wet in place, blend each span, the image held
prompt Continue the recursion loop on the ALES / Lotus edge, Lindy-first crux-first; approve the design round, make progress, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61; stop at custody gates.
think ALES192 gave the MONO reverb its most-reached-for knob — HOW MUCH reverb, the wet/dry balance — and its own recommend named the twin plainly: a stereo wet/dry mix, the same blend over both channels of a StereoClip, the image held. By Lindy-first crux-first this completes the wet/dry pair for the whole reverb family; a stereo master is what a mixing keeper actually places a voice into, so the stereo mix is the highest-Lindy tractable move on the reverb thread. It is the same shape ALES191 followed ALES190 and ALES182 followed ALES181 — a thin stereo twin over a proven mono rung.
think The shape: assert the channels enter balanced and the clock is valid, validate the mix fraction (BadMix on den = 0 or num > den), convert the span with the SAME clock.samples_for stereo_reverb_preset uses, validate against the shared channel length (BadRange) BEFORE any write, snapshot EACH channel's dry span into its own bounded stack buffer (max_clip = 4096 each), reverberate the master WET in place through ALES191's stereo_reverb_preset UNCHANGED, then blend each channel independently out[i] = saturate((den-num)·dry[i]/den + num·wet[i]/den) — the exact linear balance ALES192 proved, run per ear with NO cross-channel read, so the image the preset held is held through the blend as well.
think Six laws, each provable on both channels: the DRY EDGE (mix = 0 restores each channel to the exact dry — the identity, both ears); the WET EDGE (mix = den equals stereo_reverb_preset over the span byte for byte on both channels); the BLEND IS BETWEEN (a half mix differs from both edges and each sample of each channel is the honest weighted average dry/2 + wet/2, byte for byte against the two edges run side by side); the IMAGE IS HELD (a centred master stays identical channel-to-channel, a stereo master keeps its channels distinct — no crossing); the CHANNELS LEAVE BALANCED and silence stays silence; the FAULTS FORWARD (a bad fraction BadMix, a span past the clip DurationTooLong, an out-of-range span BadRange, both channels untouched, the two dry snapshots reads only so a refusal never mutates).
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal pass — no RED to book. TAME bans clean, width exit 0; the ALES191 stereo preset and ALES192 mono mix both re-run GREEN beside it. The only arithmetic is ALES192's proven linear blend, bounded in i64 and clamped once so it can never wrap, now run per channel with no cross-channel read; the mix a named u32/u32 fraction, not a decibel. Purely local: one StereoClip, a validated clock, ALES191's fixed banks, two bounded stack snapshots, siloed to lotus/; no socket, network, keys, funds, device, or speaker — no custody gate reached, a self-approved design round.
